  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 9 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Related Implants",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea™ series contains 3 PeriPro femur plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Proximal Femur**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Distal Femur**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Interprosthetic Femur (this topic)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pangea Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Proximal Screw Cluster**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed to offer bicortical fixation around a hip stem",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423204/images/b692dba2-8c1f-457f-9987-6cabd5dac0e6_screenshot_2025-01-08_at_11.45.52_am.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Oblong Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "To aid in plate placement and serve as an attachment site for targeter",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423204/images/6962141a-5fbf-4269-bbc1-e6ffe0c74a7e_screenshot_2025-01-08_at_11.45.44_am.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Staggered Screw Pattern**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "For effective bicortical screw placement around an intramedullary nail, hip prosthesis, or stemmed femoral component",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Cable Plug Compatible Holes**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Cable plugs accepted in any round hole and may be used in conjunction with a 2.0mm vitallium cable",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423204/images/889a9e6f-aee6-4d9b-83c1-a6afbcbf5cc9_screenshot_2025-01-08_at_11.46.11_am.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Waisted Scalloped Shape**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423204/images/d7272656-d2ca-4d62-a193-d94297c94fd9_screenshot_2025-01-08_at_11.45.48_am.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Metaphyseal Screw Cluster**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423204/images/11b2adb9-a5ff-41d8-8c41-36bd5250841b_screenshot_2025-01-08_at_11.45.39_am.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed to provide anatomic fixation through multiple distal cluster hole options depending on size of plate",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Placement",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The first dedicated interprosthetic plate designed to span from the femoral condyle to the greater trochanter to maximize plate working length",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "As the length of the plate changes, so does the radius of curvature.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The PeriPRO Femur Plating System is intended for internal fixation and stabilization of femur fractures and osteotomies, as well as, in the presence of intramedullary implants. The PeriPRO Femur Plating System is indicated for internal fixation and stabilization of femur fractures and osteotomies in normal and osteopenic bone. This includes:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Non-unions, malunions and deformities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Fracture in the presence of intramedullary implants, including periprosthetic fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Approaches",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Surgeons may choose to make an incision that spans the entire femur or combine the distal and proximal femur approaches.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
